# Private seed lives here. Never commit. (SPEC.md 5, CLAUDE.md)
.env

# Held-out split is regenerated from the private seed, never committed.
data/heldout/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Evaluation outputs are committed deliberately, not incidentally.
results/*.tmp.json

# data/dev/ is COMMITTED. Everything under it derives from the PUBLIC dev seed
# (DEV_SEED = 20260828), so it is reproducible by anyone from the seed alone and
# discloses nothing. t1_smoke.jsonl in particular must stay committed: without it the
# five tests in tests/test_env.py covering the real verifiers.v1 env and scoring path
# skip on every CI run. See CLAUDE.md, "Dev fixtures may be committed; held-out data
# never is". Held-out data is excluded above and that line is not negotiable.

# Any local env file, not just .env. A seed-bearing file must never be
# one typo away from being committed.
.env.*

# Editor swap and backup files, because a vim swap of `.env` is named `..env.swp`
# and matches NEITHER `.env` NOR `.env.*` - it starts with two dots. Such a file
# holds the full plaintext of whatever was being edited, so for `.env` that is the
# held-out seed and any API key. One was observed untracked-and-not-ignored in this
# repo on 2026-09-02 while `.env` was open in an editor; a `git add -A` at that
# moment would have committed both secrets.
.*.sw?
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.bak
*.orig

# Raw results carry per-task identity (household_id, pair_id) and regenerate in
# minutes. The .public.json sibling is the file meant to be read and quoted, so that
# is the one we keep. This also means a raw file can never be committed by reflex.
results/*.json
!results/*.public.json

# Held-out RESULTS carry the private seed: metrics.py writes run.seed verbatim,
# and every household_id/pair_id embeds it (hh-{seed}-{index}). Publishable
# aggregates are produced deliberately, never by committing a raw results file.
#
# LAST on purpose. It must override the .public.json re-inclusion above: a held-out
# public file is still a held-out artifact and does not belong in the repository.
results/*heldout*

# Model responses are partitioned by split (eval/cache.py::partition). The dev subtree
# is committed - it comes from the PUBLIC seed and is paid for, so losing it costs money.
# The held-out subtree NEVER is: each cached reply restates the household it was given, so
# committing it would publish held-out case files in all but name.
cache/responses/heldout/
